IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- THE RECORD OF EARNINGS (regulations 39 to 41).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 430 to 441.
--
-- Regulation 39 says how a contributor applies for a statement of earnings, regulation 40 how the contributor
-- is told of a reduction in the Record of Earnings, regulation 41 how the salary and wages on which a
-- contribution was made under a provincial pension plan are worked out from the contributions.
-- The rate in regulation 41 is a PER CENT figure, because the text multiplies by 100 and divides by half the rate
-- (fork F-41 in NOTES.md); every other rate in this encoding is a fraction.

§ `Part V -- the Record of Earnings (regulations 39 to 41)`

§§ `Regulation 39 -- application for a statement of earnings`

-- src:431 | 39 (1) An application under subsection 96(1) of the Act by a contributor to require the Minister to inform the contributor of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor’s account in the Record of Earnings shall be made to the Minister in writing. The application may also be made to the Minister by way of the Internet on the electronic form prescribed for that purpose and made available on the Internet.
-- src:432 | (2) An application made in writing shall include the contributor’s name, address (including the postal code) and Social Insurance Number.
-- src:433 | (3) An application made by way of the Internet shall include the contributor’s name, Social Insurance Number and postal code.
@ref Reg 39 (src:431-433)
GIVEN way IS A `cr2 Way of applying for a statement of earnings`
      `the application includes the contributor's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application includes the contributor's address, including the postal code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application includes the contributor's Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application includes the contributor's postal code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39 — an application for a statement of earnings is made as the Regulations require`
    way
    `the application includes the contributor's name`
    `the application includes the contributor's address, including the postal code`
    `the application includes the contributor's Social Insurance Number`
    `the application includes the contributor's postal code` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `an application in writing to the Minister` THEN
        `the application includes the contributor's name`
            AND `the application includes the contributor's address, including the postal code`
            AND `the application includes the contributor's Social Insurance Number`
    WHEN `an application to the Minister by way of the Internet on the electronic form prescribed for that purpose` THEN
        `the application includes the contributor's name`
            AND `the application includes the contributor's Social Insurance Number`
            AND `the application includes the contributor's postal code`
    WHEN `an application made in some other way` THEN FALSE

§§ `Regulation 40 -- notice of a reduction in the Record of Earnings`

-- src:434 | 40 Where, pursuant to subsection 97(4) of the Act, a contributor is required to be notified of a reduction in the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the account of the contributor in the Record of Earnings, the contributor shall be notified of the reduction in writing addressed to the contributor at the contributor’s latest known address.
@ref Reg 40 (src:434)
GIVEN `subsection 97(4) of the Act requires the contributor to be notified of the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 97(4) (piece cp6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40 — the contributor must be notified of the reduction in writing, addressed to the contributor's latest known address`
    `subsection 97(4) of the Act requires the contributor to be notified of the reduction` MEANS
    `subsection 97(4) of the Act requires the contributor to be notified of the reduction`

@ref Reg 40 (src:434)
GIVEN `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is addressed to the contributor at the contributor's latest known address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40 — a notice of a reduction is in writing addressed to the contributor at the latest known address`
    `the notice is in writing`
    `the notice is addressed to the contributor at the contributor's latest known address` MEANS
    `the notice is in writing` AND `the notice is addressed to the contributor at the contributor's latest known address`

§§ `Regulation 41 -- salary and wages on which a contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan`

-- src:437 | 41 (1) For the purposes of clause 53(1)(b)(ii)(A) of the Act, the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year 2019 and each subsequent year by a contributor under a provincial pension plan is an amount equal to the aggregate of all base contributions required to be made by the contributor in that year under the provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, multiplied by 100 and divided by one half of the base contribution rate for that year under the provincial pension plan.
-- src:438 | (2) For the purposes of clause 53.1(1)(b)(ii)(A) of the Act, the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year 2019 and each subsequent year by a contributor under a provincial pension plan is an amount equal to the aggregate of all first additional contributions required to be made by the contributor in that year under the provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, multiplied by 100 and divided by one half of the first additional contribution rate for that year under the provincial pension plan.
-- src:439 | (3) For the purposes of clause 53.2(1)(b)(ii)(A) of the Act, the salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year 2024 and each subsequent year by a contributor under a provincial pension plan is an amount equal to the aggregate of all second additional contributions required to be made by the contributor in that year under the provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, multiplied by 100 and divided by one half of the second additional contribution rate for that year under the provincial pension plan.
@ref Reg 41(1) (src:437)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the base contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the base contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 41(1) — the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan`
    year
    `the aggregate of the base contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan`
    `the base contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2019 AND `the base contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the aggregate of the base contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan` TIMES 100)
               DIVIDED BY (`the base contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 2))
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Reg 41(2) (src:438)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the first additional contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 41(2) — the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan`
    year
    `the aggregate of the first additional contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan`
    `the first additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2019 AND `the first additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the aggregate of the first additional contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan` TIMES 100)
               DIVIDED BY (`the first additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 2))
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Reg 41(3) (src:439)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the second additional contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 41(3) — the salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan`
    year
    `the aggregate of the second additional contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan`
    `the second additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2024 AND `the second additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the aggregate of the second additional contributions required in the year under the provincial pension plan` TIMES 100)
               DIVIDED BY (`the second additional contribution rate for the year under the provincial pension plan, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 2))
    ELSE NOTHING
